      ],
      "evidence": "stop reads running and pending in separate lock acquisitions, then calls an identity-checked termination method later. handleRemoteStop similarly matches once and re-fetches both slots. completeConsent can replace Pending with Running between those operations. Identity checks prevent terminating a different object but do not carry a Stop across that exact request transition. handleProtocolError also discards its first matched identity and re-fetches a candidate using nullable IDs.",
      "reproductionSchedule": [
        "A is pending. Local stop reads running == null and captures pending A. Pause before terminatePending acquires the lock.",
        "Consent completion acquires the lock, clears pending A and installs running A.",
        "terminatePending observes pending !== A and returns; stop then returns without terminating running A. Projection startup is still authorized, so capture can start after the local Stop.",
        "The remote path can also read running == null, race with consent completion, then read pending == null and lose the matching no-stream Stop. Separately, a nil-ID protocol rejection matched against A can re-fetch and terminate B after A completes cleanup and a new request starts."
      ],
      "impact": "An explicit Stop can be lost at consent completion and the capture may continue while the Mac keeps pulling. An ambiguous rejection can also affect a replacement request on the same connection.",
      "remediation": "Under one coordinator lock, select the matching pending/running object and perform its terminal state transition. Extract cleanup resources under that lock and cancel/purge/native-stop afterward. For an authenticated rejection, bind termination to the object matched in that same critical section rather than re-fetching with nullable IDs. Preserve cross-owner calls outside the lock.",
      "laterTest": "Coordinate Stop and consent completion at the slot handoff; either consent loses or the resulting exact request is terminal before startup. Repeat for request-only remote Stop and a nil-ID rejection paused across A cleanup/B creation.",
      "confidence": "high_source_interleaving",
      "verification": "Static source reasoning only; not reproduced by reviewer.",
      "implementationStatus": "implemented_in_frozen_followup_source_parent_validation_pending",
      "implementationReport": ".a5c/artifacts/iteration4-android-lifecycle-fixes.json"
    },
