      "evidence": "invalidate completes ticket.completion whenever lifecycle.service is null, even if markLaunchIssued already recorded a service launch. awaitQuiescence removes that completed lifecycle. A delayed onCreate/onStartCommand can therefore run after both runtime and coordinator cleanup report completion. claimStart then rejects the invalid/removed lifecycle, but onCreate already started a capture HandlerThread; stopIfUnused/onDestroy/finishCapture release it later. The same early completion can occur after service creation but before claimStart publishes service ownership.",
      "reproductionSchedule": [
        "Register and issue a start; hold delivery before claimStart registers the service.",
        "Stop the request and await coordinator/runtime quiescence. invalidate sees service == null and completes the lifecycle, so these waits can return.",
        "Deliver the held start. The service can now create its capture thread, reject the stale start and perform asynchronous teardown after the earlier cleanup result."
      ],
      "impact": "The barrier is not a guarantee that owned service startup and capture-thread lifetime have ended. This can report cleanup complete and permit a new request while the stale launch still has service work outstanding. This finding does not claim stale pixels are captured: the ticket validity checks reject native initialization.",
      "remediation": "Distinguish never-issued or failed launches from issued starts awaiting service delivery. Complete never-issued/known-failed launches immediately; retain issued launches until their delivered rejection or owned teardown acknowledges completion after the capture-thread join. Ensure the rejected-launch path can acknowledge its original ticket without authorizing projection creation.",
      "laterTest": "Hold delivery of an issued START, call Stop plus awaitQuiescence, and require the await to remain pending. Deliver the revoked start, hold its service-thread cleanup, and require completion only after that cleanup. Also cover a launch failure so failed delivery does not leave an infinite wait.",
      "confidence": "high_source_interleaving",
      "verification": "Static source reasoning only; normal emulator cleanup PASS does not cover held service delivery.",
