      "evidence": "resize increments the service captureGeneration and clears the old bitmap at line 294, then detaches/closes/resizes/reattaches native resources before notifying the coordinator at line 318. The queued frame validity closure checks only Running.captureGeneration. That coordinator value stays old through the native resize interval. The runtime generation check after encoding happened earlier and is not repeated by the outbound validity closure.",
      "reproductionSchedule": [
        "Encode an old-generation bitmap, pass the post-encode runtime check, and queue its frame behind ordinary traffic.",
        "Resize increments the service generation; hold a subsequent native resize operation before Runtime.resized.",
        "Release ordinary traffic. The frame validity callback still sees the old coordinator generation and admits the obsolete frame after the service generation changed."
      ],
      "impact": "A queued frame can dispatch from an invalidated capture generation; active old work is cancelled only after native resize finishes. The correction therefore does not yet enforce the resize boundary required by E06.",
      "remediation": "Publish the generation invalidation and cancel the old active send before blocking native resize operations. Include the actual service/runtime capture generation in response dispatch validity so the two owner values cannot leave an old queued frame admissible during publication. Keep cancellation outside the coordinator/service locks and retain the one-response/index handling.",
      "laterTest": "Hold resize after its generation increment and before resource recreation finishes. A previously queued old frame must not dispatch; the outstanding pull may produce the allowed current-generation response or idle once, without double index advancement.",
